<p>A shift runs from the cash you start with to the count at the end of the day. Every cash sale, refund and payout in between is
  counted against it, so at closing time HardPoint knows what should be in the drawer and can tell you if it's over or short.</p>

<h2>Opening a shift</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Open the till. If no shift is open on it, HardPoint asks for one first.</li>
  <li>Count the change in the drawer and type it in <strong>Cash in the drawer to start</strong>.</li>
  <li>Press <strong>Open shift</strong>.</li>
</ol>
<p>A shift belongs to the till, not to one person. Each till has one open shift at a time, and cashiers who switch in with their PIN sell
  into the same shift. Each sale still records who rang it up, and the report shows who opened and who closed the shift.</p>

<h2>Cash in and out during the day</h2>
<p>Press <strong>Shift</strong> in the till's top bar, then <strong>Cash drop / payout</strong>. Choose what's happening, type the amount
  and a reason, and press <strong>Record</strong>:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Drop to the safe</strong>: takings taken out of the drawer.</li>
  <li><strong>Pay out</strong>: cash paid from the till, for transport or a supplier, say.</li>
  <li><strong>Pay in</strong>: more change added to the float.</li>
</ul>
<p>Cash movements go on the till this device is set to, since that's the drawer the cash is in. A payout above the shop's limit
  (KES 5,000 to start with; owners change it under <strong>Settings › Shop details</strong>) needs an owner's or manager's approval PIN,
  and <strong>Settings › Activity</strong> records who approved it.</p>
<p>Each one shows on the shift report with its reason. On tills that print through QZ Tray, <strong>Open drawer</strong> in the top bar opens
  the drawer without a sale. It's logged as "No sale" in <strong>Settings › Activity</strong>.</p>

<h2>The X report</h2>
<p>Press <strong>Shift</strong> on the till at any time to see the <strong>X report</strong>: how the shift is doing so far, without closing it.
  It shows sales, voids, discounts and tax; takings by method (cash, card, M-Pesa, on account, and Airtel Money or foreign cash when used);
  deposits and account payments; refunds; and the cash drawer worked out line by line. <strong>Print</strong> prints it.</p>

<h2>Closing the shift</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Finish or clear any sale still open or parked on the till. The shift won't close while one has goods on it.</li>
  <li>On the shift, press <strong>Close shift</strong>. Cashiers can also use <strong>End my shift</strong> on their Home.</li>
  <li>Count all the cash and type it in <strong>Cash counted</strong>. If the till takes dollars or other currencies, count each one's notes
    separately in its own box.</li>
  <li>Add a <strong>Note</strong> if the manager should know something, then press <strong>Close shift</strong> and confirm.</li>
</ol>
<p>The count is blind: the closing page doesn't show what's expected. Afterwards the <strong>Z report</strong> shows the expected cash,
  what was counted, and whether the drawer is <strong>Over</strong>, <strong>Short</strong> or <strong>Balanced</strong>, with the same for
  each foreign currency. Press <strong>Print</strong> to print it. Once closed, nothing more can be sold on that till until a new shift is
  opened.</p>

<%= render "help/walkthrough", tour: HelpTour.find("close-shift") %>

<h2>What's expected in the drawer</h2>
<p>The opening float, plus cash sales, cash deposits on orders and cash account payments, less cash refunds, change given for foreign
  notes, payouts and drops, plus pay-ins. M-Pesa, Airtel Money and card takings are listed on the report but don't count towards the drawer.</p>

<h2>Past shifts</h2>
<p><strong>Sell › Shifts</strong> lists shifts with the till, branch, who opened and closed them, and the over or short. Owners and managers
  see every till; cashiers see the shifts of the till they're on. Open one to see its X or Z report. The
  <strong>Shifts and cash counts</strong> report lists every closed shift in a period. See
  <%= link_to "Reports and the owner's dashboard", help_article_path("reports"), class: "link" %>.</p>

<h2>Shifts left open</h2>
<p>On the owner's Home, <strong>Cash in the drawers</strong> shows the cash expected in every open till. A shift still open from an earlier
  day shows under <strong>Needs you today</strong>; press <strong>See shifts</strong> and close it so the cash gets counted.</p>
<p>For the till itself, see <%= link_to "Selling at the till", help_article_path("selling"), class: "link" %>; for dollars, see
  <%= link_to "Dollars and other currencies", help_article_path("foreign-currencies"), class: "link" %>.</p>
